{"name":"Carona","hex":"#fba52e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[],"entries":[{"title":"Carona, Lombardy","blocks":[{"text":"Carona is a comune (municipality) in the Province of Bergamo in the Italian region of Lombardy, located about 80 kilometres (50 mi) northeast of Milan and about 35 kilometres (22 mi) north of Bergamo. By the statute of Carona, on its territory there are no hamlets, but it still recognises the localities of Carona Bassa and Pagliari."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Carona_panorama.jpg/330px-Carona_panorama.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carona%2C_Lombardy","wikidata":"Q100151"},{"title":"Carona, Ticino","blocks":[{"text":"Carona is a former municipality in the district of Lugano in the canton of Ticino in Switzerland. On 14 April 2013 the former municipalities of Bogno, Cadro, Carona, Certara, Cimadera, Valcolla and Sonvico merged into the municipality of Lugano."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Carona.JPG/330px-Carona.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carona%2C_Ticino","wikidata":"Q68453"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/Carona_%26_Lake.JPG/500px-Carona_%26_Lake.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/Carona_%26_Lake.JPG/500px-Carona_%26_Lake.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Carona and its lake","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACarona_%26_Lake.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Ciona.JPG/500px-Ciona.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Ciona.JPG/1280px-Ciona.JPG?u